Absolutely amazing game. For me, an easy 9.9/10 (minus 0.1
). What sold it to me at first was the bit about exploring super massive structures...And waow I was not disappointed. I had never played a game like this ever before. In fact it was quite an experience at times. The really bizarre feeling of wandering among huge abandoned structures was really something. It's like living in a Kafka's novel. Plus the soundtrack (unfortunately not available) is very very good. Fits perfectly the game. A great bunch of alternative/indie artists !
I'd highly recommend this game to whoever wants to experience something different. Hats off to the developers (Limasse Five) for offering such a great bit of indie game. I hope they're working on a sequel.

This is THE most amount of fun I've ever had playing co-op.  Originally bought this on the Xbox 360, had a blast there and the PC port just delivers the fun on better graphics and higher framerates.  What's not to like?
Only thing that I still dislike the game for is the experience system, mostly due to it basically saying "Don't put any points into strength."  How the experience gain works is that, for every hit you make on an enemy that's alive, you get 1 experience point.  Doesn't matter if your swing does 30 damage or 90, you only get 1 experience point, so in order to get a decent amount of levels, you have to spend your points elsewhere.  Apart from that, it's still an amazing game nonetheless.
Make sure to grab a 4-pack though.  Nothing's more fun than fighting a boss to free a princess, then fighting each other to see who gets the kiss.  Protip: Focus Red Knight, especially if he's put points into his magic.  You'll thank me later c;

Well Team 17 bring nostalgia back up again. Worms is one of the greatest franchises of the gaming history.
Pros:
- Super backgrounds;
- Awesome story;
- Worms and Booms;
Cons:
- The tutorial part is just a bit grindy (not a word), and dull, but after that, you are good to go, and to have a Lot of fun, Also do the challenges. Simply great.

I've played all of the arcade metal slugs and i have to say that when i heard it was coming to steam i thought it would be a nice "flashback" of the good old days but i was so wrong about it that i decided to leave a review as a heads up for metal slug fans.
Pros
- Game includes all the characters, enemies, vehicles, bosses and items that we all know from all the other metal slug games;
- Game currency is very easy and fast to earn so you can upgrade your units and base almost at the same rate you progress on the world map;
- It's easy to get the hang of it after a few minutes of playtime;
- For a free to play tower defense like game it has much more content than many other TD games;
Cons
- There is much P2W stuff in the game and the coolest stuff is only unlocked with real money;
- PVP system takes forever to find an opponent so you'll be limited to the single player campaign;
- Even if the enemies and the scenario keep changing in many levels it feels repetitive after playing for some time;
- The game's ammo system (wich works like energy in many games) takes a long time to refill and without ammo you can't play anything on the world map and are limited to pvp and like said above pvp system takes forever to find an opponent so you have a limited amount of tries before waiting for it to refill before trying your luck again.
I love games where skill is the most important thing in them, and it saddens me to see that this ***** was the best they could do with this awesome franchise.
I'm sorry but i cannot recommend a game that in my opinion should only exist on tablets and cellphones to any computer user.
I give it 3/10

A great game! Its setting really puts you into the island with the characters, and its crazy texts are equally cool!
Pros:
- Great story, a mix of thriller/adventure in a 2D game;
- Cool and well done dubbing;
- You can sometimes take photos with your friends (one thing that makes me have shivers);
- Right-sized map, full of easter-eggs and achievements;
Cons:
- Sometimes the walking system bugs (but you just have to use one more directional key to make it work again);
- The walking speed is a bit too real, you spend much time to walk around the island.

I understand why people rage at this game, but I like "Defense games" and this genre is themed with Metal Slug.
From Screen Shots I saw that this was a copy paste port, but this port does not affect game play it affects features and touch inputs like "touch here to start". It also can be labeled as Pay to Win, I can see that too but it can be played without paying like I'm doing. I think it's good and addicting. Needs a proper PC patch.
+
Great pixelated visuals like the usual from SNK Metal Slug series;
A lot of levels, random events to play;
Upgradeable base and units;
Online ranked and friends, 1on1 or 2on2 matches.
-
You need credits which loads over time to play, so you have to stop playing while waiting;
A lazy port from a mobile touch platform;
Even missing features from that mobile port;
Simple options settings.
Edit: It got patched for M&K and controller inputs.
Score: 6/10.

