The game shows the signs of age, but nonetheless a good remark about some aspects that RPGs usually don't take into account.
Pros:
+ Good gameplay, with a wide range of possible strategies to afford enemies;
+ Environment can (must) be used; also, good stealth mechanism;
+ Multiple endings: now we're all used to it, but back in the time it must have been awesome and it's right to give it the right credit.
Cons:
- Lack of secondary quests and lore - set aside the choices for the endings, the storyline is straightforward;
- Few customization options for the character's skills;
- Poor enemy IA, counterbalanced by high damage output - no way to be tank;
- The story is nothing new under the sun.
There might be other pros and cons, but the main ones are here. Recommended, for the nostalgic or the "collector" who wants to see with his eyes an RPG which gives importance to the environment (I'm both).

Like many gamers, I've played a lot of Minecraft - it's hard not to compare the two, as they have a lot in common. In short; if you loved Minecraft, you'll probably love this too, but there are differences for sure;
The main difference, and the biggest selling point for me, is the community. I've seen plenty of community projects in Minecraft, but nothing like this. In Boundless players organically settle beside one another and form settlements, they set up trade networks and assist each other with the games unqiue Portal mechanic - allowing seamless travel between far away planets.
I'm dumbfounded this game hasn't had more attention. The more people that know about this game the better. It gets a definite thumbs up from me!
